    {
      "component_id": "ED26-BM-RAT2021-4-3-C03",
      "verdict": "partial",
      "gap": "The source's historical claims about the measures are absent: D as MacColl's delta (1897, via Keynes), Q as W. E. Johnson's coefficient of influence and Carnap's relevance quotient (n.8), L commended by Peirce, Turing and Good, QL from Good (1950), KO from Kemeny-Oppenheim (1952), Z from Crupi-Tentori (2013), MCIE from Good (1960) and Heckerman (1988) (pp.270-271). The named old-evidence reconstructions (Glymour 1980; Jeffrey 2004; Earman 1992, Fitelson-Hartmann 2015; Hajek-Joyce 2008; p.267) are described without attribution. Steel's (2003) normative argument that POP-D is needed for enumerative induction (p.271) is missing, and the editorial note that Merin died in 2019 with final revisions by the editors (p.274) is not recorded. Without these the chapter does not separate the source's historical claims from its formal and normative ones.",
